  {:id "core:2870" :draft "core" :line 2870 :level :must :section "trust-posture-in-ps-asserted-access" :text "The PS MUST protect its signing keys with appropriate rigor — compromise of a PS's signing key allows forgery of identity claims for every resource that accepts that PS." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2876" :draft "core" :line 2876 :level :should :section "person-token-exposure" :text "The PS bounds it further: it decides whether to issue at all, and SHOULD treat the first person token for a given resource as requiring the person's approval (#person-token-endpoint)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2882" :draft "core" :line 2882 :level :must :section "continuity-not-proofing" :text "The protocol does not state what standard, if any, a PS applied before recognizing a person, and a resource MUST NOT infer one (#person-tokens)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2886" :draft "core" :line 2886 :level :may :section "person-token-org-policy" :text "The OPTIONAL `tenant` claim declares the organization the person belongs to, and unlike `sub` it is not directed — the same value appears at every resource the organization's agents reach." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2890" :draft "core" :line 2890 :level :must :section "person-token-org-policy" :text "`tenant` is organizational context and MUST NOT be treated as part of the person's identifier, which is `(iss, sub)` (#directed-identifiers)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2896" :draft "core" :line 2896 :level :must :section "person-token-not-authorization" :text "Implementations MUST check `typ` before acting on any AAuth JWT, and MUST reject `aa-person+jwt` where an auth token is required (#person-token-verification)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2896.2" :draft "core" :line 2896 :level :should :section "person-token-not-authorization" :text "Deployments SHOULD test this case explicitly; it fails open." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2902" :draft "core" :line 2902 :level :should :section "incremental-consent" :text "A PS SHOULD present the accumulated picture — the approved description together with the updates already accepted — when asking the person to accept another, rather than the increment alone." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2908" :draft "core" :line 2908 :level :must :section "ps-approval-endpoint-auth" :text "When the PS approval/consent endpoint is reachable beyond a single-user local deployment, the PS MUST authenticate the approving party before acting on a consent or denial decision." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2914" :draft "core" :line 2914 :level :must :section "agent-person-binding" :text "The PS MUST ensure that each agent is associated with exactly one person." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2916" :draft "core" :line 2916 :level :should :section "agent-person-binding" :text "The PS recognizes a returning agent by `(agent_token.iss, agent_token.sub)`; on first interaction with a new tuple for a person, the PS SHOULD treat it as a new-agent enrollment and surface this clearly at the consent screen, displaying the agent provider's name and logo (from agent provider metadata) alongside any agent-supplied display values (`platform`, `device`) provided in the request." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2916.2" :draft "core" :line 2916 :level :must :section "agent-person-binding" :text "Once established, the PS MUST NOT allow a different person to claim the same agent." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2916.3" :draft "core" :line 2916 :level :must :section "agent-person-binding" :text "If an agent's association needs to change (e.g., an employee leaves an organization), the existing binding MUST be revoked and a new binding established." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2929" :draft "core" :line 2929 :level :must :section "ps-as-high-value-target" :text "PS implementations MUST apply appropriate security controls including access control, audit logging, and monitoring." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2931" :draft "core" :line 2931 :level :may :section "ps-as-high-value-target" :text "The PS MAY delegate authentication to an identity provider chosen by the person or organization (e.g., an enterprise IdP via OIDC federation), reducing the PS's role in credential management." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2931.2" :draft "core" :line 2931 :level :may :section "ps-as-high-value-target" :text "The PS MAY also delegate policy evaluation to external services selected by the person, so that consent and authorization decisions are not solely determined by the PS operator." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2935" :draft "core" :line 2935 :level :must :section "tls-requirements" :text "All HTTPS connections MUST use TLS 1.2 or later, following the recommendations in BCP 195 [@!RFC9325]." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2941" :draft "core" :line 2941 :level :should :section "non-repudiation-and-audit-after-key-rotation" :text "Deployments that require durable audit or non-repudiation beyond a key's lifetime SHOULD capture the evidence at verification time, while the key is still discoverable, rather than relying on re-verification later:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2947" :draft "core" :line 2947 :level :must :section "non-repudiation-and-audit-after-key-rotation" :text "These measures trade privacy for durability: archived signatures and keys are correlatable, so deployments MUST balance audit retention against the privacy-preserving properties of short-lived keys and directed identifiers (#privacy-considerations), and apply appropriate retention limits and access controls." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2955" :draft "core" :line 2955 :level :should :section "directed-identifiers" :text "The PS SHOULD provide a pairwise pseudonymous user identifier (`sub`) per resource, preventing resources from correlating users across trust domains." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2957" :draft "core" :line 2957 :level :must :section "directed-identifiers" :text "A `sub` MUST be unique within the issuer, so `(iss, sub)` identifies the person unambiguously and `tenant` is never part of the identifier." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2957.2" :draft "core" :line 2957 :level :must :section "directed-identifiers" :text "The same value MUST be used in the person token (#person-token-structure), in the resource token the resource derives from it, and in every auth token issued for that resource, and MUST NOT vary with the agent or its key." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2965" :draft "core" :line 2965 :level :must :section "ps-visibility" :text "PS implementations MUST apply appropriate access controls and data retention policies." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:2999" :draft "core" :line 2999 :level :must :section "http-authentication-scheme-registration" :text "The token MUST be bound to an HTTP Message Signature — the `authorization` field MUST be included in the signature's covered components." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3019" :draft "core" :line 3019 :level :must :section "link-relation-type-registration" :text "- Notes: The target MUST be a server identifier followed by `/.well-known/aauth-resource.json`; recipients verify the document against the URL it was fetched from and do not use the relation for key discovery." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3422" :draft "core" :line 3422 :level :must :section "minimal-ps" :text "The floor is the four REQUIRED fields (#ps-metadata): `issuer`, `jwks_uri`, `person_token_endpoint`, and `auth_token_endpoint`." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3422.2" :draft "core" :line 3422 :level :should :section "minimal-ps" :text "A `revocation_endpoint` is RECOMMENDED, since it is how the person's agent provider tells the PS to stop honoring an agent (#token-revocation)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3430" :draft "core" :line 3430 :level :may :section "minimal-ps" :text "The `url` can be a page the PS serves, but it need not be visited: the PS MAY complete the interaction over a channel it already has — a notification the person taps, a message they reply to — and the code is consumed at that completion (#user-interaction)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3468" :draft "core" :line 3468 :level :may :section "why-no-agent-identifier" :text "The agent token still reaches the AS, because a resource deploys an AS to have policy evaluated and an agent token MAY carry claims bearing on that — attestation, platform integrity, workload identity." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3538" :draft "core" :line 3538 :level :may :section "why-ps-reports-nothing-to-ap" :text "The person is the party the rule protects, so a PS MAY report the per-recipient outcome to them." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3618" :draft "core" :line 3618 :level :may :section "why-not-extend-www-authenticate" :text "A `401` response MAY include multiple headers, and the client uses whichever it understands:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "core:3626" :draft "core" :line 3626 :level :may :section "why-not-extend-www-authenticate" :text "A `402` response MAY include `WWW-Authenticate` for payment (e.g., the Payment scheme ([@?I-D.ryan-httpauth-payment])) alongside `Accept-Signature-Scheme` for authentication or `AAuth-Requirement` for authorization:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "key:155" :draft "key" :line 155 :level :must :section "signature-key-http-request-header" :text "A verifier that selects a member whose scheme token it does not implement, including any unregistered value, MUST reject the request with a `Signature-Error` of `error=unsupported_scheme` ((#unsupported-scheme)) and MUST NOT fail in a scheme-specific or undefined manner." :suite-clauses ["sigkey.v.unknown-scheme" "sigkey.v.missing-member-jwt" "sigkey.v.missing-member-hwk" "sigvec.reject.unknown-scheme"] :scenarios ["sigkey-unknown-scheme" "sigkey-missing-member-jwt" "sigkey-missing-member-hwk" "sigvec.reject-unknown-scheme"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "key:155.2" :draft "key" :line 155 :level :should :section "signature-key-http-request-header" :text "Verifiers SHOULD dispatch on the scheme token through a lookup over the HTTP Signature-Key Scheme registry ((#scheme-registry)) rather than a fixed set of branches, so that unknown schemes take this defined path." :suite-clauses ["sigkey.v.unknown-scheme" "sigkey.v.missing-member-jwt" "sigkey.v.missing-member-hwk" "sigvec.reject.unknown-scheme"] :scenarios ["sigkey-unknown-scheme" "sigkey-missing-member-jwt" "sigkey-missing-member-hwk" "sigvec.reject-unknown-scheme"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
