  {:id "budgets:461" :draft "budgets" :line 461 :level :must :section "budget-consumed" :text "A resource MUST NOT include `budget_consumed` unless `budget` is present in the same token, and MUST omit it rather than state it in another scale — a record carried in a stale scale is the thousandfold error (#errors) in miniature." :suite-clauses ["budget.consumption"] :scenarios ["budget-consumption"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:463" :draft "budgets" :line 463 :level :should :section "budget-consumed" :text "A resource issuing a resource token on a challenge to a request that carried an auth token SHOULD include the record." :suite-clauses ["budget.consumption"] :scenarios ["budget-consumption"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:475" :draft "budgets" :line 475 :level :should :section "ps-token-endpoint" :text "An agent seeking a larger budget obtains a fresh resource token from the resource — stating the larger figure in the authorization endpoint request (#authorization-endpoint), or being handed one on a `401` (#exhaustion) — and SHOULD explain the need in the `justification` parameter of the auth token request." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:491" :draft "budgets" :line 491 :level :should :section "ps-inputs" :text "Four inputs are available at the moment of the decision, and a PS applying the person's policy SHOULD use all of them:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:515" :draft "budgets" :line 515 :level :may :section "ps-responses" :text "A PS that sees consumption running ahead of what the mission implies MAY return `202` with `requirement=clarification` ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Clarification Required), putting a question to the agent before deciding." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:538" :draft "budgets" :line 538 :level :must :section "ps-responses" :text "A PS that puts a budget to the person for consent MUST present the amount as a human-readable figure in its unit — \"$5.00\", not `{5000000, USD, 6}` — visually distinct from any resource-supplied description, which is Markdown and MUST be sanitized before rendering (#budget-units)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:546" :draft "budgets" :line 546 :level :may :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "**`budget`** (OPTIONAL): A budget object (#budget-object) carrying the ceiling the PS will allow." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:568" :draft "budgets" :line 568 :level :must :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "The PS MUST copy `unit` and `decimals` from the resource token's `budget` claim unchanged, and MUST NOT set `amount` higher than the resource token's `budget.amount`." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:568.2" :draft "budgets" :line 568 :level :must :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "The AS MUST NOT issue a `budget` claim exceeding this parameter, and MAY lower it further." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:570" :draft "budgets" :line 570 :level :must :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "When the AS returns an auth token, the PS MUST verify, along with the checks of the base protocol's Auth Token Delivery, that the token carries a `budget` claim when the PS sent a `budget` parameter, that the claim has the `unit` and `decimals` of that parameter and an `amount` no higher, and that the token carries no `budget` claim when the PS sent no `budget` parameter." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:572" :draft "budgets" :line 572 :level :must :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "When the resource token carries `budget` and the PS omits this parameter, the AS MUST NOT issue a `budget` claim." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:572.2" :draft "budgets" :line 572 :level :must :section "as-token-endpoint" :text "A PS that grants the resource's full offer says so by echoing the resource token's `budget`; omission is what a PS that does not implement this extension sends, and it MUST NOT be read as a grant." :suite-clauses ["budget.four-party-grant" "budget.four-party-omission"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-four-party-omission" "budget-consumption" "budget-header" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:578" :draft "budgets" :line 578 :level :may :section "auth-token" :text "**`budget`** (OPTIONAL): A budget object (#budget-object)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:601" :draft "budgets" :line 601 :level :must :section "auth-token" :text "- The issuer MUST copy `unit` and `decimals` from the resource token's `budget` claim unchanged." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:602" :draft "budgets" :line 602 :level :must :section "auth-token" :text "- The issuer MUST NOT set `amount` higher than the resource token's `budget.amount`, or, in four-party access, higher than the `budget` parameter of the PS-to-AS token request (#as-token-endpoint)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:603" :draft "budgets" :line 603 :level :must :section "auth-token" :text "- An issuer MUST NOT include `budget` in an auth token when the resource token carried no `budget` claim." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:607" :draft "budgets" :line 607 :level :must :section "auth-token" :text "- A resource that issued a `budget` in a resource token and receives an auth token without a `budget` claim MUST treat the request as carrying no budget authorization under this extension and apply its own default." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:608" :draft "budgets" :line 608 :level :must :section "auth-token" :text "- A resource MUST enforce against the auth token's `unit` and `decimals`, not against its own current `budget_units` metadata." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:621" :draft "budgets" :line 621 :level :must :section "aauth-budget-header" :text "- **`remaining`** (REQUIRED): A non-negative Integer, in the granted scale, giving what is left of the budget on this auth token, net of reservations for requests in flight (#overshoot)." :suite-clauses ["budget.header"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:622" :draft "budgets" :line 622 :level :may :section "aauth-budget-header" :text "- **`cost`** (OPTIONAL): A non-negative Integer, in the granted scale, giving what **this request** cost." :suite-clauses ["budget.header"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:623" :draft "budgets" :line 623 :level :may :section "aauth-budget-header" :text "- **`reserved`** (OPTIONAL): A non-negative Integer, in the granted scale, giving what the resource has held against the grant for this request and not yet committed (#overshoot)." :suite-clauses ["budget.header"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:623.2" :draft "budgets" :line 623 :level :must :section "aauth-budget-header" :text "REQUIRED where `cost` is omitted (#cost-omitted)." :suite-clauses ["budget.header"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
