  {:id "budgets:692" :draft "budgets" :line 692 :level :must :section "cost-omitted" :text "A resource MUST NOT omit both `cost` and `reserved`." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:696" :draft "budgets" :line 696 :level :may :section "trailer-rules" :text "A resource MAY send `AAuth-Budget` as a trailer field, subject to three rules:" :suite-clauses ["budget.trailer"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:698" :draft "budgets" :line 698 :level :must :section "trailer-rules" :text "The response MUST list `AAuth-Budget` in a `Trailer` header field ([@!RFC9110], Section 6.6.1)." :suite-clauses ["budget.trailer"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:699" :draft "budgets" :line 699 :level :must :section "trailer-rules" :text "A trailer instance MUST NOT restate a member the header instance carried." :suite-clauses ["budget.trailer"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:700" :draft "budgets" :line 700 :level :must :section "trailer-rules" :text "A recipient MUST NOT treat the trailer as necessary." :suite-clauses ["budget.trailer"] :scenarios ["budget-header"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:710" :draft "budgets" :line 710 :level :must :section "ambiguous-failure" :text "The agent MUST assume the request cost as much as the resource had held for it: `reserved` where it saw one, and otherwise the request's maximum cost as the resource would have bounded it (#overshoot)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:710.2" :draft "budgets" :line 710 :level :should :section "ambiguous-failure" :text "It carries that assumption until a later response's `remaining` supersedes it, and it SHOULD NOT retry a chargeable request before then." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:714" :draft "budgets" :line 714 :level :should :section "ambiguous-failure" :text "That is application-layer and does not provide the application independence this header exists for, so a resource that emits it and can also send a trailer SHOULD send both." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:724" :draft "budgets" :line 724 :level :must :section "exhaustion" :text "A request refused under this section MUST NOT draw down the budget or appear in the record and counters." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:726" :draft "budgets" :line 726 :level :should :section "exhaustion" :text "The fresh resource token SHOULD carry the presented token's consumption record (#budget-consumed), its spend to date — the context for deciding whether to authorize more, and the figure that tells the issuer how much of the refused allocation was actually consumed." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:730" :draft "budgets" :line 730 :level :should :section "reason-parameter" :text "A resource challenging because the budget is exhausted rather than because the token expired SHOULD include a `reason` parameter on the `requirement` member:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:745" :draft "budgets" :line 745 :level :may :section "reason-parameter" :text "For either value, the enclosed resource token MAY carry a `budget` sized for what the resource would need to see granted." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:749" :draft "budgets" :line 749 :level :should :section "required-member" :text "A resource refusing under `insufficient-budget` has computed the request's maximum cost — (#overshoot) requires it to, before serving — and SHOULD report that figure as the `required` member of `AAuth-Budget`:" :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:761" :draft "budgets" :line 761 :level :should :section "required-member" :text "`required` is not the same figure as the `budget` claim of the enclosed resource token, and the two SHOULD differ." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:763" :draft "budgets" :line 763 :level :may :section "required-member" :text "A resource MAY refuse without `required` — where the operation has no cost bound it is willing to state, or where stating it would disclose pricing the resource does not publish." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:765" :draft "budgets" :line 765 :level :must :section "required-member" :text "The base protocol says an agent that does not recognize a `requirement` value MUST NOT treat the response as satisfiable and surfaces it as an error, while recipients MUST ignore unknown *parameters* on the `requirement` member ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Requirement Responses)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:771" :draft "budgets" :line 771 :level :may :section "exhaustion-deferred" :text "A resource MAY deliver either refusal as a `202` deferred response rather than a `401`, holding the invocation ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Deferred Delivery)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:790" :draft "budgets" :line 790 :level :must :section "exhaustion-deferred" :text "For the held invocation, the resource MUST NOT reserve against or meter to the token presented on the original request." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:793" :draft "budgets" :line 793 :level :must :section "exhaustion-deferred" :text "A resource answering a repeated presentation of the completing token from the stored result, as the base protocol requires, MUST NOT meter the invocation a second time." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:815" :draft "budgets" :line 815 :level :may :section "requires-auth-token" :text "It MAY continue to serve unmetered endpoints on a person token, since a resource MAY apply different modes to different endpoints ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Resource Access Modes)." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:815.2" :draft "budgets" :line 815 :level :must :section "requires-auth-token" :text "A resource MUST NOT rely on this extension for an endpoint it serves without an auth token." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:831" :draft "budgets" :line 831 :level :must :section "unreported-allocations" :text "Until a figure arrives, the issuer MUST account for the allocation as fully consumed." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:853" :draft "budgets" :line 853 :level :may :section "settlement" :text "The issuer cannot tell which of the two it has, so it holds the allocation reserved until `exp` and MAY revoke again later." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:857" :draft "budgets" :line 857 :level :should :section "settlement" :text "An issuer whose ceiling is per calendar period SHOULD set each allocation's `exp` no later than the period boundary." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:863" :draft "budgets" :line 863 :level :must :section "aggregation" :text "It is the `budget` claim of the token presented, and (#overshoot) states the invariant: committed consumption plus outstanding reservations against *that token* MUST NOT exceed *its* granted `amount`." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:865" :draft "budgets" :line 865 :level :must :section "aggregation" :text "The resource MUST aggregate consumption against the key `(ps, sub, aud)` of the auth token, which is what the consumption record (#budget-consumed) and the usage counters (#usage-counters) report." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:867" :draft "budgets" :line 867 :level :must :section "aggregation" :text "A resource MUST NOT refuse a request that fits its token's budget because a per-person total has reached some figure the resource inferred; no party told it such a figure, and the budgets it was handed are what it was authorized to honor." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:889" :draft "budgets" :line 889 :level :may :section "billing-account" :text "Account Binding ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Account Binding) carries the answer: an OPTIONAL `account` parameter on the authorization endpoint request, named from the resource's own namespace, echoed as the `account` claim of the resource token and copied into the auth token." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:901" :draft "budgets" :line 901 :level :must :section "concurrency" :text "- A resource MUST apply the reserve-commit-release invariant of (#overshoot) atomically per auth token, so that concurrent requests presenting the same token cannot together exceed its budget." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:902" :draft "budgets" :line 902 :level :must :section "concurrency" :text "- A resource MUST post consumption to the `(ps, sub, aud)` ledger (#aggregation) atomically, so that concurrent requests across different tokens do not lose or double-count against the record and counters." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:903" :draft "budgets" :line 903 :level :should :section "concurrency" :text "- A PS SHOULD size per-token budgets so that their sum stays within whatever standing ceiling it holds for the person at that resource." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:909" :draft "budgets" :line 909 :level :must :section "overshoot" :text "A resource MUST NOT let metered consumption exceed the granted `amount`." :suite-clauses ["budget.hard-cap"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-consumption" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:911" :draft "budgets" :line 911 :level :must :section "overshoot" :text "An operation with no finite cost bound MUST be given one, be truncated when the remainder is consumed, or be refused." :suite-clauses ["budget.hard-cap"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-consumption" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:913" :draft "budgets" :line 913 :level :must :section "overshoot" :text "The normative requirement is the invariant, not the mechanism: committed consumption plus outstanding reservations MUST NOT exceed the granted `amount` at any moment, including under concurrent requests (#concurrency)." :suite-clauses ["budget.hard-cap"] :scenarios ["budget-four-party-grant" "budget-consumption" "budget-hard-cap"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:919" :draft "budgets" :line 919 :level :must :section "failed-calls" :text "Whatever it meters, the record and counters MUST reflect, or the person's numbers will not reconcile with the bill." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
  {:id "budgets:937" :draft "budgets" :line 937 :level :must :section "usage-request" :text "The caller — a person server, or in four-party access an access server — MUST make a signed POST to the `usage_endpoint`, signing as a server in its own right: an HTTP Sig under the `jwks_uri` scheme, with `id` its `issuer` and `dwk` its metadata document ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Keying Material), and the signature additionally covering `content-type` and `content-digest`, as on a request with a body to a PS or AS ([@!I-D.hardt-oauth-aauth-protocol], Covered Components)." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage-request"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:945" :draft "budgets" :line 945 :level :may :section "usage-request" :text "and one OPTIONAL member:" :suite-clauses ["budget.usage-request"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:951" :draft "budgets" :line 951 :level :must :section "usage-request" :text "REQUIRED when the caller is an access server and the request carries a scope key, since the tokens an AS issues carry values from every person server that federates with it." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage-request"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:953" :draft "budgets" :line 953 :level :must :section "usage-request" :text "A request MUST carry a scope key or `jkts`, and MAY carry both." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage-request"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:997" :draft "budgets" :line 997 :level :must :section "usage-response" :text "- **`as_of`** (REQUIRED): The time through which the figures are complete, in seconds since the Unix epoch." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:997.2" :draft "budgets" :line 997 :level :may :section "usage-response" :text "Metering aggregation MAY lag serving; `as_of` is what keeps a lagging figure honest." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:998" :draft "budgets" :line 998 :level :must :section "usage-response" :text "- **`aud`** (REQUIRED): The caller the response was produced for — a person server, identified as in the `ps` claim of a resource token, or an access server, identified as in the `iss` claim of an auth token." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:999" :draft "budgets" :line 999 :level :must :section "usage-response" :text "- **`unit`** (REQUIRED) and **`decimals`** (REQUIRED): The unit every figure in the response is denominated in, and its scale, as in the budget object (#budget-object)." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1001" :draft "budgets" :line 1001 :level :must :section "usage-response" :text "- **`usage`** (REQUIRED when the request carried a scope key): Calendar counters for that scope." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1002" :draft "budgets" :line 1002 :level :must :section "usage-response" :text "- **`jkts`** (REQUIRED when the request carried `jkts`): An object mapping each thumbprint to what that key consumed (#per-key)." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1011" :draft "budgets" :line 1011 :level :must :section "calendar-counters" :text "- **`all_time`** (REQUIRED): everything the resource has metered against budgets under this key." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1015" :draft "budgets" :line 1015 :level :may :section "calendar-counters" :text "The calendar counters other than `all_time` are OPTIONAL; a resource omits periods it does not track." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1015.2" :draft "budgets" :line 1015 :level :may :section "calendar-counters" :text "For a `mission_s256` query, `all_time` is the mission total — the figure a PS wants when deciding whether to fund a mission's continuation — and a resource MAY serve it alone." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1027" :draft "budgets" :line 1027 :level :should :section "per-key" :text "A resource SHOULD retain a key's figure for at least 24 hours after that key's last metered request, and MAY retain it longer." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1029" :draft "budgets" :line 1029 :level :must :section "per-key" :text "A resource MUST omit a thumbprint from `jkts` rather than report zero for it when it holds no figure — because the key is unrecognized, or because its figure has been pruned." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1039" :draft "budgets" :line 1039 :level :should :section "signed-response" :text "Signing the usage response is RECOMMENDED." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1039.2" :draft "budgets" :line 1039 :level :must :section "signed-response" :text "The signature MUST cover `@status`, `content-type`, and `content-digest`, and MUST be bound to the request by covering the request's `@authority` and `@path` with the `req` parameter ([@!RFC9421])." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1057" :draft "budgets" :line 1057 :level :must :section "signed-response" :text "It is RECOMMENDED rather than REQUIRED because the figures are decision context rather than authorization, and because this would be the first response-side signature in the AAuth family — the signature profile is request-side throughout (#header-trust)." :suite-clauses ["budget.usage"] :scenarios ["budget-usage"] :status {:aauth-go :pass :aauth-rust :pass}}
  {:id "budgets:1063" :draft "budgets" :line 1063 :level :must :section "usage-authorization" :text "The resource MUST only answer for values that have appeared in auth tokens it accepted whose `iss` or `ps` claim names the caller: for a PS, the tokens it issued in three-party access and the tokens carrying it as `ps` in four-party access; for an AS, the tokens it issued, and for a scope key only those whose `ps` is the request's `ps`." :suite-clauses [] :scenarios []}
